Gradle is powerful tool used to compile the project.
It run the project & download the dependencies

useful commands.
./gradlew tasks
It gives list of all things that our project is able to do

for doing specific task

./gradlew tasks | grep -i apollo
It gives all things related to apollo in the project

eg:-
./gradlew tasks | grep -i compile
./gradlew tasks | grep -i kotlin
./gradlew :hello:tasks --all | grep -i kotlin

We have to include all directories in settings.gradle.kts
file so that it is considered as module and gradle can go there and can pick those
run command ./gradlew project
Note: you need to sync android studio after that


gradle only compile all files having extension .kt

libs.version.toml file is used to manage dependencies

we can use same dependencies versions in more than 1 module as well

if you want that one module/project in your project communicates with another module/project
add that module/project in dependency by below example
Here I want hello module to use some function present in rick module so I need to add rick module here
implementation(project(":rick"))
